#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198180 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198282 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0809c075-e1be-5d49-b1fe-5433114bcf16" :knowledge-point/title "\"If-Then\", \"If\", \"Only If\", and \"Implies\""}] :question/id #uuid "d20f2ac9-3190-5c58-a0a5-ddcd8c3f5817" :question/math-academy-id "e-13234" :question/problem "Consider the following predicates:\n\n$\\qquad$ $P(x):$ $x$ is prime $\\qquad$ $Q(x):$ $x$ is not a multiple of $10$\n\nWhich of the following expresses the conditional predicate $P(x) \\Rightarrow Q(x)?$\n\n- $x$ is not a multiple of $10$ if $x$ is prime\n\n- If $x$ is not a multiple of $10,$ then $x$ is prime\n\n- $x$ is prime implies $x$ is not a multiple of $10$\n\n- $x$ is not a multiple of $10$ only if $x$ is prime" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the following grammatical constructions for the implication $P\\Rightarrow Q{:}$\n\n- If $P,$ then $Q$\n\n- $P$ only if $Q$\n\n- $Q$ if $P$\n\n- $P$ implies $Q$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Option I reads\n![](images/48/482e156a7d3aef3f75a6b51efec5069fc48696749d7f580d4e40d7801a41f90a.svg)\nwhich corresponds to $P(x) \\Rightarrow Q(x).$ $\\:{\\color{green}\\checkmark}$\n\n- Option II reads\n![](images/fb/fb19cec758144f4ae3ca6580d5171757369a831f6cfc7d940fa95fcfaf2522b9.svg)\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x) \\Rightarrow P(x).$ $\\:{\\color{red}\\times}$\n\n- Option III reads\n![](images/1f/1f472c122fe745e97fb31328625eccb71515dfee4b99e4bba548bf367cc8cc78.svg)\nwhich corresponds to $P(x) \\Rightarrow Q(x).$ $\\:{\\color{darkgreen}\\checkmark}$\n\n- Option IV reads\n![](images/52/525a046232143aa333ded66fb2bec55ff0011a8f76ef74373b9c6c99abdc3fd3.svg)\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x) \\Rightarrow P(x).$ $\\:{\\color{red}\\times}$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198185 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198285 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c614609-dae7-5cde-a26a-52104d47ebf5" :knowledge-point/title "Biconditionals"}] :question/id #uuid "f4b354bf-6629-5574-9674-fdc3ca707b0a" :question/math-academy-id "e-13273" :question/problem "Express $P \\Leftrightarrow Q$ as a sentence given the following:\n\n- $P:$ $A \\cup B = A.$\n\n- $Q:$ $B \\subseteq A.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the following grammatical constructions for the biconditional $P\\Leftrightarrow Q{:}$\n\n- $P$ if and only if $Q$\n\n- $P$ iff $Q$\n\n- $P$ is necessary and sufficient for $Q$\n\n- $P$ is equivalent to $Q$\n\n- If $P$ then $Q,$ and conversely\n\nTherefore, some correct grammatical constructions of $P \\Leftrightarrow Q$ are the following:\n\n- $A \\cup B = A$ **if and only if** $B \\subseteq A.$\n\n- $A \\cup B = A$ **iff** $B \\subseteq A.$\n\n- $A \\cup B = A$ **is necessary and sufficient for** $B \\subseteq A.$\n\n- $A \\cup B = A$ **is equivalent to** $B \\subseteq A.$\n\n- **If** $A \\cup B = A,$ **then** $B \\subseteq A,$ **and conversely**."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198187 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198283 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0c26aeaa-9252-5bd3-9ad6-0fc25ca6b03c" :knowledge-point/title "Necessary and Sufficient Conditions"}] :question/id #uuid "8ba22130-b8bb-55d0-83b0-5a3b89bcf876" :question/math-academy-id "e-13275" :question/problem "Complete the following table:\n\n| Sentence | Symbolic Form |\n| --- | --- |\n| $B$ is sufficient for $A$ |  |\n| For $A,$ it is sufficient that $B$ |  |\n| $B$ is necessary for $A$ |  |\n| For $A,$ it is necessary that $B$ |  |" :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $S \\Rightarrow N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\textbf{S}\\textrm{ufficient} \\: \\Rightarrow \\: \\textbf{N}\\textrm{ecessary}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nWe have the following grammatical constructions for $S\\Rightarrow N{:}$\n\n- $S$ is sufficient for $N$\n\n- For $N,$ it is sufficient that $S$\n\n- $N$ is necessary for $S$\n\n- For $S,$ it is necessary that $N$\n\nLet's now compare these against the entries in our table:\n\n- \"$B$ is sufficient for $A$\" means $B\\Rightarrow A.$\n\n- \"For $A,$ it is sufficient that $B$\" means $B\\Rightarrow A.$\n\n- \"$B$ is necessary for $A$\" means $A\\Rightarrow B.$\n\n- \"For $A,$ it is necessary that $B$\" means $A\\Rightarrow B.$\n\nThe completed table is shown below.\n\n| Sentence | Symbolic Form |\n| --- | --- |\n| $B$ is sufficient for $A$ | $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}B\\Rightarrow A}$ |\n| For $A,$ it is sufficient that $B$ | $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}B\\Rightarrow A}$ |\n| $B$ is necessary for $A$ | $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}A\\Rightarrow B}$ |\n| For $A,$ it is necessary that $B$ | $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}A\\Rightarrow B}$ |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198188 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198284 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b24ae815-5706-5b65-bab8-2d67f8405c9c" :knowledge-point/title "\"Whenever\", and \"Provided That\""}] :question/id #uuid "c776807d-efab-534b-b79c-582e4906bb4b" :question/math-academy-id "e-13276" :question/problem "Consider the following predicates:\n\n$\\qquad$ $P(x):$ $x\\in\\mathbb {Z}^{-}$ $\\qquad$ $Q(x):$ $x$ is negative\n\nWhich of the following expresses the conditional predicate $P(x) \\Rightarrow Q(x)?$\n\n- Whenever $x$ is negative, then $x\\in\\mathbb {Z}^{-}$\n\n- $x$ is negative whenever $x\\in\\mathbb {Z}^{-}$\n\n- $x$ is negative, provided that $x\\in\\mathbb {Z}^{-}$" :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $P \\Rightarrow Q$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- Whenever $P,$ then $Q$\n\n- $Q$ whenever $P$\n\n- $Q,$ provided that $P$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Option I reads\n![](images/21/21fd3acc1e0a8862b0010d28252278e204bfe6c25abb66aed01f31cc0a565642.svg)\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x) \\Rightarrow P(x).$ $\\:{\\color{red}\\times}$\n\n- Option II reads\n![](images/44/4436567914aa607eae98ac50a467d6d6be1715d7b1f9cdfa0f907dc0df8b99ba.svg)\nwhich corresponds to $P(x) \\Rightarrow Q(x).$ $\\:{\\color{green}\\checkmark}$\n\n- Option III reads\n![](images/30/305d426cb7c241d68ab4576848ae519429b58e3ae655cb65c23dc74c09d0722e.svg)\nwhich corresponds to $P(x) \\Rightarrow Q(x).$ $\\:{\\color{green}\\checkmark}$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198699 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198285 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c614609-dae7-5cde-a26a-52104d47ebf5" :knowledge-point/title "Biconditionals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37046a87-18c5-507f-bc35-a399578045cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ is even or $4$ is divisible by $2.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421025} {:answer/id #uuid "48628bed-966b-5e82-a7ec-d2c0f8647a12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ is even and $4$ is divisible by $2.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421036} {:answer/id #uuid "99a4a2a4-0fa6-55cb-9516-a6da6381f1c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ is even only if $4$ is divisible by $2.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421060} {:answer/id #uuid "a00e2dfe-e552-51bc-9a13-9c47db99cf73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ is even if and only if $4$ is divisible by $2.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421067} {:answer/id #uuid "aa30bfac-4d0d-532b-9f89-0d0c454c4300" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ is even if $4$ is divisible by $2.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421072}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a00e2dfe-e552-51bc-9a13-9c47db99cf73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ is even if and only if $4$ is divisible by $2.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421067} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ede0371-77c4-5012-b41f-556acaac28ec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194820}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ceecdafd-e8f8-565d-8402-4e6510683f49" :question/math-academy-id "q-171412" :question/problem "Express $A⇔B$ as a sentence given the following:\n\n- $A:$ $4$ is even.\n\n- $B:$ $4$ is divisible by $2.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the following grammatical constructions for the biconditional $P⇔Q:$\n\n- $P$ if and only if $Q$\n\n- $P$ iff $Q$\n\n- $P$ is necessary and sufficient for $Q$\n\n- $P$ is equivalent to $Q$\n\n- If $P$ then $Q,$ and conversely\n\nTherefore, among the given options, the correct grammatical construction of $A⇔B$ is the following:\n\n$\\,$ $4$ is even **if and only if** $4$ is divisible by $2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421144 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198285 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c614609-dae7-5cde-a26a-52104d47ebf5" :knowledge-point/title "Biconditionals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ae6d9e6-00c4-5ee5-bc3f-ec52b0c0dc4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x$ is positive is equivalent to $x>0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421026} {:answer/id #uuid "3c23cefd-456f-5f0f-941c-8d48c26de887" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x$ is positive if $x>0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421028} {:answer/id #uuid "401381c3-e289-5f7e-b008-96dcdfd5d85d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x$ is positive or $x>0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421033} {:answer/id #uuid "54dc99bd-e45d-56d3-8b2c-a9cf11872588" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x$ is positive, provided that $x>0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421038} {:answer/id #uuid "aae41545-3194-5698-95df-6153f725ed0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x$ is positive implies $x>0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421074}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ae6d9e6-00c4-5ee5-bc3f-ec52b0c0dc4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x$ is positive is equivalent to $x>0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421026} :answer-field/id #uuid "03206bc2-9e2d-59db-a5f3-be01edc94740" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421106}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4c8d7440-4eac-56af-a31b-85c3ab92c898" :question/math-academy-id "q-171416" :question/problem "Express $P(x)⇔Q(x)$ as a sentence given the following notations:\n\n- $P(x):$ $x$ is positive.\n\n- $Q(x):$ $x>0.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the following grammatical constructions for the biconditional $P⇔Q:$\n\n- $P$ if and only if $Q$\n\n- $P$ iff $Q$\n\n- $P$ is necessary and sufficient for $Q$\n\n- $P$ is equivalent to $Q$\n\n- If $P$ then $Q,$ and conversely\n\nTherefore, among the given options, the grammatical construction of $P(x)⇔Q(x)$ is the following:\n\n$\\,$ $x$ is positive **is equivalent to** $x>0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421143 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198285 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c614609-dae7-5cde-a26a-52104d47ebf5" :knowledge-point/title "Biconditionals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f5bb8ac-767a-5871-92a9-37dddfee9d64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A triangle is right and it has two complementary angles." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421013} {:answer/id #uuid "58aef142-5159-5aa0-94fe-d7e18c41a235" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A triangle has two complementary angles only if it is a right triangle." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421040} {:answer/id #uuid "5fc85f2a-aa86-597d-9f3c-026f5190527b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A triangle is right if and only if it has two complementary angles." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421043} {:answer/id #uuid "9522521b-1b5e-5d5c-ac86-1c40f78398bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A triangle is right, provided that it has two complementary angles." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421057} {:answer/id #uuid "c7595d95-071f-5d6e-8261-384302cfad91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A triangle has two complementary angles, if it is a right triangle." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421087}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5fc85f2a-aa86-597d-9f3c-026f5190527b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A triangle is right if and only if it has two complementary angles." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421043} :answer-field/id #uuid "852a81f7-8616-56ae-ae1c-84fc0268a724" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421118}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "204c3d5d-7433-5e9d-bacd-9011685dc6a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-171419" :question/problem "Express $P⇔Q$ as a sentence given the following:\n\n- $P:$ $A$ triangle is right.\n\n- $Q:$ $A$ triangle has two complementary angles." :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the following grammatical constructions for the biconditional $P⇔Q:$\n\n- $P$ if and only if $Q$\n\n- $P$ iff $Q$\n\n- $P$ is necessary and sufficient for $Q$\n\n- $P$ is equivalent to $Q$\n\n- If $P$ then $Q,$ and conversely\n\nTherefore, among the given options, the correct grammatical construction of $P⇔Q$ is the following:\n\n$\\,$ A triangle is right **if and only if** it has two complementary angles."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198847 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198284 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b24ae815-5706-5b65-bab8-2d67f8405c9c" :knowledge-point/title "\"Whenever\", and \"Provided That\""}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a4619cbe-1c36-5f99-873f-13cb7863c361" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A⇒B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186196151} {:answer/id #uuid "3cd65873-374b-5673-bc6a-d210ac0617b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B⇒A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186196152}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a4619cbe-1c36-5f99-873f-13cb7863c361" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A⇒B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186196151} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4536466-f002-5f74-85bc-88ae6548edd8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186196150} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bb169ed-cf62-5d1c-9e0c-552daa676b9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A⇒B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186196154} {:answer/id #uuid "1699e7eb-49e1-5b54-a5eb-5a1703dc856b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B⇒A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186196155}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0bb169ed-cf62-5d1c-9e0c-552daa676b9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A⇒B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186196154} :answer-field/id #uuid "168603f7-7186-557a-a8ff