}} | $A⇒B$ |\n| {{field-2}} | $A⇒B$ |\n| {{field-3}} | $B⇒A$ |\n| {{field-4}} | $A⇒B$ |" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the following grammatical constructions for the implication $P⇒Q:$\n\n- If $P,$ then $Q$\n\n- $P$ only if $Q$\n\n- $Q$ if $P$\n\n- $P$ implies $Q$\n\nLet's now compare these against the entries in our table:\n\n- \"If $A,$ then $B$\" means $A⇒B$\n\n- \"$A$ only if $B$\" means $A⇒B$\n\n- \"$A$ if $B$\" means $B⇒A$\n\n- \"$A$ implies $B$\" means $A⇒B$\n\nThe completed table is shown below.\n\n| Sentence | Symbolic Form |\n| --- | --- |\n| If $A,$ then $B$ | $A⇒B$ |\n| $A$ only if $B$ | $A⇒B$ |\n| $A$ if $B$ | $B⇒A$ |\n| $A$ implies $B$ | $A⇒B$ |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421142 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198282 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0809c075-e1be-5d49-b1fe-5433114bcf16" :knowledge-point/title "\"If-Then\", \"If\", \"Only If\", and \"Implies\""}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "093f27fc-7e6f-5b74-9e0f-56f1dcd8da8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421004} {:answer/id #uuid "27753478-b4dc-5f6b-9f5d-e4c8cf0b2741" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421016} {:answer/id #uuid "4cf28c27-5628-51c2-afd9-674c7904768f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421037} {:answer/id #uuid "5e1f026b-b1a3-571d-937c-f08cf77e8b6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421042} {:answer/id #uuid "a241a06c-b9b1-53dc-aa4f-bc3f27232754" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421068}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e1f026b-b1a3-571d-937c-f08cf77e8b6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421042} :answer-field/id #uuid "7423f83a-bd3f-57b5-a6e1-9ee4c5646676" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421115}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0e0b252f-632c-5fb4-955e-f2c2686886d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-183448" :question/problem "$\\,$ $P(x):$ $x=2$ $\\,$ $Q(x):$ ${x}^{2}=4$\n\nConsider the predicates $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ above. Which of the following expresses the conditional predicate $P(x)⇒Q(x)?$\n\n- ${x}^{2}=4$ implies $x=2$\n- If ${x}^{2}=4,$ then $x=2$\n- ${x}^{2}=4$ only if $x=2$\n- ${x}^{2}=4$ if $x=2$" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the following grammatical constructions for the implication $P⇒Q:$\n\n- If $P,$ then $Q$\n\n- $P$ only if $Q$\n\n- $Q$ if $P$\n\n- $P$ implies $Q$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Option I reads\n\n$$\n{{{x}^{2}=4}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\\,\\text{implies}\\,{{x=2}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x)⇒P(x).$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- Option II reads\n\n$$\n\\text{if}\\,{{{x}^{2}=4}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)},\\,\\text{then}\\,{{x=2}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x)⇒P(x).$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- Option III reads\n\n$$\n{{{x}^{2}=4}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\\,\\text{only if}\\,{{x=2}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x)⇒P(x).$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- Option IV reads\n\n$$\n{{{x}^{2}=4}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\\,\\text{if}\\,{{x=2}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $P(x)⇒Q(x).$ $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"IV only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421153 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198283 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0c26aeaa-9252-5bd3-9ad6-0fc25ca6b03c" :knowledge-point/title "Necessary and Sufficient Conditions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id