d #uuid "3e1432d2-b89f-57dd-a8d9-a53d86ec88ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A⇒B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421030} :answer-field/id #uuid "9eb88832-ac8c-5502-8207-ce8fa8b6e43d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421122} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0320ab27-8c91-593f-863f-a330a38d6971" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B⇒A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421002} {:answer/id #uuid "163033c6-267c-510a-879d-d8d2a5dd6ceb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A⇒B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421010}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "163033c6-267c-510a-879d-d8d2a5dd6ceb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A⇒B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421010} :answer-field/id #uuid "e2f43cd8-654f-514d-b93e-2c9c4d481c4a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421132}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c2b5afd8-4be0-5217-be25-bcd0b5c0bdf4" :question/math-academy-id "q-183490" :question/problem "Find the missing values in the following table:\n\n| Sentence | Symbolic Form |\n| --- | --- |\n| $A$ is sufficient for $B$ | {{field-1}} |\n| For $B,$ it is sufficient that $A$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $B$ is necessary for $A$ | {{field-3}} |\n| For $B,$ it is necessary that $A$ | {{field-4}} |" :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nWe have the following grammatical constructions for $S⇒N:$\n\n- $S$ is sufficient for $N$\n\n- For $N,$ it is sufficient that $S$\n\n- $N$ is necessary for $S$\n\n- For $S,$ it is necessary that $N$\n\nLet's now compare these against the entries in our table:\n\n- \"$A$ is sufficient for $B$\" means $A⇒B.$\n\n- \"For $B,$ it is sufficient that $A$\" means $A⇒B.$\n\n- \"$B$ is necessary for $A$\" means $A⇒B.$\n\n- \"For $B,$ it is necessary that $A$\" means $B⇒A.$\n\nThe completed table is shown below.\n\n| Sentence | Symbolic Form |\n| --- | --- |\n| $A$ is sufficient for $B$ | $A⇒B$ |\n| For $B,$ it is sufficient that $A$ | $A⇒B$ |\n| $B$ is necessary for $A$ | $A⇒B$ |\n| For $B,$ it is necessary that $A$ | $B⇒A$ |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198858 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198283 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0c26aeaa-9252-5bd3-9ad6-0fc25ca6b03c" :knowledge-point/title "Necessary and Sufficient Conditions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60e0be5d-31e1-5e6c-9b9d-7be47926bca6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "For $A,$ it is necessary that $B$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421044} {:answer/id #uuid "82d9ed58-92df-51b0-8f6a-20e5f0f9c9c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "For $B,$ it is necessary that $A$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421052}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82d9ed58-92df-51b0-8f6a-20e5f0f9c9c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "For $B,$ it is necessary that $A$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421052} :answer-field/id #uuid "475f6e42-2d48-5b68-b3a0-f02dfae17a47" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186196278} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "943361cd-dd23-5e0b-a6fd-9850a1c0a23b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/iden