ues in the following table:\n\n| Sentence | Symbolic Form |\n| --- | --- |\n| {{field-1}} | $A⇒B$ |\n| {{field-2}} | $A⇒B$ |\n| {{field-3}} | $B⇒A$ |\n| {{field-4}} | $B⇒A$ |" :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nWe have the following grammatical constructions for $S⇒N:$\n\n- $S$ is sufficient for $N$\n\n- For $N,$ it is sufficient that $S$\n\n- $N$ is necessary for $S$\n\n- For $S,$ it is necessary that $N$\n\nLet's now compare these against the entries in our table:\n\n- \"$A$ is sufficient for $B$\" means $A⇒B.$\n\n- \"For $B,$ it is sufficient that $A$\" means $A⇒B.$\n\n- \"$A$ is necessary for $B$\" means $B⇒A.$\n\n- \"For $B,$ it is necessary that $A$\" means $B⇒A.$\n\nThe completed table is shown below.\n\n| Sentence | Symbolic Form |\n| --- | --- |\n| $A\\text{ is sufficient for }B$ | $A⇒B$ |\n| $\\text{For }B,\\text{ it is sufficient that }A$ | $A⇒B$ |\n| $A\\text{ is necessary for }B$ | $B⇒A$ |\n| $\\text{For }B,\\text{ it is necessary that }A$ | $B⇒A$ |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198859 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198283 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0c26aeaa-9252-5bd3-9ad6-0fc25ca6b03c" :knowledge-point/title "Necessary and Sufficient Conditions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b0822caf-5b2d-5d87-ba6c-81e288ccc593" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186196291} {:answer/id #uuid "b0df2b74-895f-5174-8953-8d4ed3d57fd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186196292} {:answer/id #uuid "0fb1a477-6708-584e-8d47-1f28bcca55c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186196293} {:answer/id #uuid "1a8958c2-0597-58ee-8feb-2e7d57eb8027" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186196294} {:answer/id #uuid "2283f4ab-474b-589a-b24f-afa516d783bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186196295}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0fb1a477-6708-584e-8d47-1f28bcca55c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186196293} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ae68f40-20e6-597a-a9b7-9dac54c3c828" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186196290}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "587a7a92-f47b-5043-840d-bba7363fe179" :question/math-academy-id "q-183495" :question/problem "$\\,$ $P(x):$ $6\\,|\\,x$ $\\,$ $Q(x):$ $3\\,|\\,x$\n\nConsider the predicates $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ above. Which of the following expresses the conditional predicate $P(x)⇒Q(x)?$\n\n- $6\\,|\\,x$ is sufficient for $3\\,|\\,x$\n- For $3\\,|\\,x,$ it is sufficient that $6\\,|\\,x$\n- $6\\,|\\,x$ is necessary for $3\\,|\\,x$\n- For $6\\,|\\,x,$ it is necessary that $3\\,|\\,x$" :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nWe have the following grammatical constructions for $S⇒N:$\n\n- $S$ is sufficient for $N$\n\n- For $N,$ it is sufficient that $S$\n\n- $N$ is necessary for $S$\n\n- For $S,$ it is necessary that $N$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Option I reads\n\n$$\n{{6\\,|\\,x}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\\,\\text{is sufficient for}\\,{{3\\,|\\,x}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $P(x)⇒Q(x).$ $\\,✓$\n\n- Option II reads\n\n$$\n\\text{for}\\,{{3\\,|\\,x,}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\\,\\text{it is sufficient that}\\,{{6\\,|\\,x}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $P(x)⇒Q(x).$ $\\,✓$\n\n- Option III reads\n\n$$\n{{6\\,|\\,x}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\\,\\text{is necessary for}\\,{{3\\,|\\,x}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x)⇒P(x).$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- Option IV reads\n\n$$\n\\text{for}\\,{{6\\,|\\,x,}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\\,\\text{it is necessary that}\\,{{3\\,|\\,x}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $P(x)⇒Q(x).$ $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II and IV only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421141 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198283 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0c26aeaa-9252-5bd3-9ad6-0fc25ca6b03c" :knowledge-point/title "Necessary and Sufficient Conditions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ef0d8fa-6fbc-553b-b26f-6d47fc529632" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421008} {:answer/id #uuid "a92c8a27-c90f-55ba-900b-012f540a5175" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, III and IV" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421071} {:answer/id #uuid "ac43712d-08c1-5314-bc53-7add8e989850" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, III and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421075} {:answer/id #uuid "b2a82ac1-260b-5de1-9737-cad96665d7a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421082} {:answer/id #uuid "fb5963c4-6280-5a68-adcd-4bcc40dceab0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421100}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb5963c4-6280-5a68-adcd-4bcc40dceab0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421100} :answer-field/id #uuid "f88db5da-74c7-5a6c-8f64-068574198241" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421138}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "03f10976-674d-5f7f-9c6a-ec5de8c4e5cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-183510" :question/problem "$\\,$ $P(x):$ $x=-1$ $\\,$ $Q(x):$ $(x-1)(x+1)=0$\n\nConsider the predicates $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ above. Which of the following expresses the conditional predicate $P(x)⇒Q(x)?$\n\n- $x=-1$ is sufficient for $(x-1)(x+1)=0$\n- $x=-1$ is necessary for $(x-1)(x+1)=0$\n- For $(x-1)(x+1)=0,$ it is necessary that $x=-1$\n- For $x=-1,$ it is sufficient that $(x-1)(x+1)=0$" :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nWe have the following grammatical constructions for $S⇒N:$\n\n- $S$ is sufficient for $N$\n\n- For $N,$ it is sufficient that $S$\n\n- $N$ is necessary for $S$\n\n- For $S,$ it is necessary that $N$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Option I reads\n\n$$\n{{x=-1}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\\,\\text{is sufficient for}\\,{{(x-1)(x+1)=0}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $P(x)⇒Q(x).$ $\\,✓$\n\n- Option II reads\n\n$$\n{{x=-1}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\\,\\text{is necessary for}\\,{{(x-1)(x+1)=0}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x)⇒P(x).$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- Option III reads\n\n$$\n\\text{for}\\,{{(x-1)(x+1)=0,}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\\,\\text{it is necessary that}\\,{{x=-1}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x)⇒P(x).$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- Option IV reads\n\n$$\n\\text{for}\\,{{x=-1,}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\\,\\text{it is sufficient that}\\,{{(x-1)(x+1)=0}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x)⇒P(x).$ $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421147 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198284 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b24ae815-5706-5b65-bab8-2d67f8405c9c" :knowledge-point/title "\"Whenever\", and \"Provided That\""}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d6844ae-27ea-5374-a438-c24d7e669095" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A⇒B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421007} {:answer/id #uuid "1bdadf87-28de-5f43-b22e-91359b75ecaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B⇒A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421012}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1bdadf87-28de-5f43-b22e-91359b75ecaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B⇒A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421012} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc6f13fe-2a99-5d7e-ae68-45d38a11565e" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421130} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a72e058-271b-5aa6-80fa-533e0bbc2a15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B⇒A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421019} {:answer/id #uuid "b46318ad-fba0-55d4-96a7-2a0d90f45007" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A⇒B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421083}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b46318ad-fba0-55d4-96a7-2a0d90f45007" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A⇒B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421083} :answer-field/id #uuid "e38ec42d-bc75-5c8d-9cc7-a3f9b8