er\", and \"Provided That\""}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d40fcad-2b54-5f09-b54d-9a821f10c93a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421006} {:answer/id #uuid "29ff0373-60cd-5181-92d4-2b66865dbf72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421018} {:answer/id #uuid "988b9e54-2317-550f-8181-5d56c55e2bc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421059} {:answer/id #uuid "e436142a-6fc6-52cb-bacc-09d95d051cd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421095} {:answer/id #uuid "fe58e7c2-f1a1-57fe-86bd-e109566044a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421105}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d40fcad-2b54-5f09-b54d-9a821f10c93a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421006} :answer-field/id #uuid "88cc20d1-1323-5c7b-9afb-5b2500b0cb08" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421120}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "50849cc0-0b42-5b52-abb5-e0bdf56880ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-183568" :question/problem "$\\,$ $P(x):$ $0\\le x<1$ $\\,$ $Q(x):$ $|x|<1$\n\nConsider the predicates $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ above. Which of the following expresses the conditional predicate $P(x)⇒Q(x)?$\n\n- Whenever $|x|<1,$ then $0\\le x<1$\n- $0\\le x<1$ whenever $|x|<1$\n- $|x|<1,$ provided that $0\\le x<1$" :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $P⇒Q$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- Whenever $P,$ then $Q$\n\n- $Q$ whenever $P$\n\n- $Q,$ provided that $P$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Option I reads\n\n$$\n\\text{Whenever}\\,{{|x|<1}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)},\\,\\text{then}\\,{{0\\le x<1}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x)⇒P(x).$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- Option II reads\n\n$$\n{{0\\le x<1}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\\,\\text{whenever}\\,{{|x|<1}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x)⇒P(x).$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- Option III reads\n\n$$\n{{|x|<1\\text{,}}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\\,\\text{provided that}\\,{{0\\le x<1}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $P(x)⇒Q(x).$ $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421155 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198285 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c614609-dae7-5cde-a26a-52104d47ebf5" :knowledge-point/title "Biconditionals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07315abd-4baf-524a-b2c5-1f7b344c1673" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "If $P,$ then $Q$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421003} {:answer/id #uuid "17fd888b-1ea6-5604-b6e0-f6f3f825750e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$P$ is equivalent to $Q$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421011} {:answer/id #uuid "250f345e-efdc-555d-86b3-1484ff4bb330" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$P$ if and only if $Q$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421015} {:answer/id #uuid "acdeafa2-7d88-5bdd-874d-59c9ac65fb88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$P$ is necessary and sufficient for $Q$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421077} {:answer/id #uuid "cdc4dea6-6991-521b-be88-3f03c1368bc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$P$ iff $Q$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421090}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07315abd-4baf-524a-b2c5-1f7b344c1673" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "If $P,$ then $Q$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421003} :answer-field/id #uuid "e38359ba-08a7-5f5b-a1d0-eef3255ecbb7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421133}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f00a0a1e-c589-5b06-8786-738dfcf01ab1" :question/math-academy-id "q-183639" :question/problem "Which of the following is **NOT** a grammatical construction for the biconditional $P⇔Q?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the following grammatical constructions for the biconditional $P⇔Q:$\n\n- $P$ if and only if $Q$\n\n- $P$ iff $Q$\n\n- $P$ is necessary and sufficient for $Q$\n\n- $P$ is equivalent to $Q$\n\n- If $P$ then $Q,$ and conversely\n\nFrom the given options, the only one that is NOT a grammatical construction for $P⇔Q$ is \"If $P,$ then $Q$\" (this is the grammatical construction of $P⇒Q).$"}]}
